r scientific genius. <strong>Turing</strong>, the father of computing, makes a wonderfully unique wise name.\"}}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nature's Wise Names 🌿\"]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Nature provides its own symbols of wisdom. <strong>Owl</strong> is the universal symbol of wisdom — perfect for a bird or any pet with knowing eyes. Trees, ancient and patient, offer <strong>Oak</strong>, <strong>Elder</strong>, <strong>Sequoia</strong>, <strong>Banyan</strong>, <strong>Bodhi</strong> (the tree of enlightenment).\"}}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Mountains evoke eternal wisdom: <strong>Everest</strong>, <strong>Denali</strong>, <strong>Fuji</strong>, <strong>Olympus</strong>. The moon, silent and knowing, inspires <strong>Luna</strong>, <strong>Selene</strong>, <strong>Chandra</strong>. Elephants, renowned for their memory and wisdom, suggest <strong>Ganesha</strong> (Hindu god of wisdom), <strong>Hathi</strong>, <strong>Babar</strong>.\"}}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Global Wisdom Names 🌍\"]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Languages around the world offer beautiful wisdom names. Japanese: <strong>Chie</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Satoshi</strong> (wise, clear-thinking), <strong>Kenji</strong> (wise, intelligent). Chinese: <strong>Zhi</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Ming</strong> (bright, wise). Sanskrit: <strong>Bodhi</strong> (awakening, enlightenment), <strong>Prajna</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Veda</strong> (knowledge).\"}}]\n30:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"C