s\"}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 list-none pl-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[1,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#classical\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Classical Wisdom Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[2,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#literary\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Literary & Philosophical Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[3,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#nature\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Nature's Wise Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#global\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Global Wisdom Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Some animals radiate intelligence — the watchful \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"49\",{\"href\":\"/animal/owl/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Owl\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", the calculating \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"72\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Cat\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", the problem-solving \",\"$La\",\", the curious \",\"$Lb\",\". A name that means wisdom honors your pet's mental gifts and celebrates their thoughtful nature. This guide explores wisdom-names from ancient philosophy to modern literature.\"]}],\"$Lc\",\"$Ld\",\"$Le\",\"$Lf\",\"$L10\",\"$L11\",\"$L12\",\"$L13\",\"$L14\",\"$L15\",\"$L16\",\"$L17\"]}],\"$L18\",\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\"]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"$L1e\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$1f\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@20\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"99\",{\"href\":\"/animal/dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Dog\",\" Name Generator\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"118\",{\"href\":\"/animal/parrot/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Parrot\",\" Name Generator\"]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Classical Wisdom Names 🏛️\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"The ancient world gave us timeless wisdom names. <strong>Athena</strong>, Greek goddess of wisdom, is the ultimate smart-pet name. <strong>Minerva</strong>, her Roman counterpart, offers similar gravitas. <strong>Sophia</strong>, the Greek word for wisdom itself, has been cherished for millennia. <strong>Solomon</strong>, the biblical king known for his wisdom, makes a dignified name for a calm, intelligent pet.\"}}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Other classical wisdom names: <strong>Sage</strong> (wise one), <strong>Thoth</strong> (Egyptian god of wisdom), <strong>Odin</strong> (Norse god who sacrificed an eye for wisdom), <strong>Mimir</strong> (Norse being of knowledge). The name <strong>Plato</strong> brings philosophical gravitas, while <strong>Oracle</strong> suggests prophetic knowing.\"}}]\nf:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Literary & Philosophical Names 📚\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Literature and philosophy give us some of the wisest-sounding names. <strong>Gandalf</strong> (wise wizard), <strong>Dumbledore</strong> (headmaster of wisdom), <strong>Yoda</strong> (Jedi master of wisdom), <strong>Atticus</strong> (wise father in To Kill a Mockingbird). <strong>Merlin</strong>, the legendary wizard, embodies magical wisdom.\"}}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Philosophical names: <strong>Buddha</strong> (enlightened one), <strong>Lao</strong> (after Lao Tzu), <strong>Rumi</strong> (wise poet), <strong>Seneca</strong> (Stoic philosopher). <strong>Newton</strong>, <strong>Einstein</strong>, <strong>Curie</strong>, and <strong>Hawking</strong> honor scientific genius. <strong>Turing</strong>, the father of computing, makes a wonderfully unique wise name.\"}}]\n12:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nature's Wise Names 🌿\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Nature provides its own symbols of wisdom. <strong>Owl</strong> is the universal symbol of wisdom — perfect for a bird or any pet with knowing eyes. Trees, ancient and patient, offer <strong>Oak</strong>, <strong>Elder</strong>, <strong>Sequoia</strong>, <strong>Banyan</strong>, <strong>Bodhi</strong> (the tree of enlightenment).\"}}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Mountains evoke eternal wisdom: <strong>Everest</strong>, <strong>Denali</strong>, <strong>Fuji</strong>, <strong>Olympus</strong>. The moon, silent and knowing, inspires <strong>Luna</strong>, <strong>Selene</strong>, <strong>Chandra</strong>. Elephants, renowned for their memory and wisdom, suggest <strong>Ganesha</strong> (Hindu god of wisdom), <strong>Hathi</strong>, <strong>Babar</strong>.\"}}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Global Wisdom Names 🌍\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Languages around the world offer beautiful wisdom names. Japanese: <strong>Chie</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Satoshi</strong> (wise, clear-thinking), <strong>Kenji</strong> (wise, intelligent). Chinese: <strong>Zhi</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Ming</strong> (bright, wise). Sanskrit: <strong>Bodhi</strong> (awakening, enlightenment), <strong>Prajna</strong> (wisdom), <strong>Veda</strong> (knowledge).\"}}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Celtic wisdom: <strong>Fionn</strong> (fair, wise), <strong>Senan</strong> (little wise one). Arabic: <strong>Hakeem</strong> (wise), <strong>Rashid</strong> (rightly guided). Hebrew: <strong>Chochma</strong> (wisdom). Native American: <strong>Nokomis</strong> (grandmother, wise woman). African: <strong>Akili</strong> (wisdom, intelligence in Swahili), <strong>Zuri</strong> (beautiful and wise).\"}}]\n18:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I know if a wisdom name suits my pet?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Watch your pet's behavior — animals who pause to observe, solve puzzles, learn quickly, or seem to 'think' before acting suit wisdom names perfectly. But any beloved pet deserves a name you find meaningful.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are wisdom names too serious for playful pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Not at all! The contrast between a playful pet and a profound name like Socrates or Bodhi creates wonderful character. A silly dog named Plato is both endearing and memorable.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What's the most popular wisdom-inspired pet name?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Athena and Sage are currently the most popular wisdom names for pets globally. Both are short, beautiful to say, and carry clear meaning without being overly serious.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I use a philosopher's name even if I haven't read their work?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The name itself carries cultural weight and meaning. You don't need to be a philosophy scholar to appreciate the wisdom association of names like Plato or Rumi. What matters is how the name feels to you.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"owl\",{\"href\":\"/animal/owl/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦉\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Owl\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"elephant\",{\"href\":\"/animal/elephant/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐘\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Elephant\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"cat\",{\"href\":\"/animal/cat/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🐱\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Cat\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"parrot\",{\"href\":\"/animal/parrot/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover